# 7. Electronics Assembly

## Step 1 – Install Raspberry Pi

Secure the Raspberry Pi to the mounting points inside the enclosure.

Do not overtighten screws.

---

## Step 2 – Install TFT Display

Connect the TFT display using the appropriate interface.

Mount the display facing upward toward the optical system.

---

## Step 3 – Install Camera

Attach the Raspberry Pi Camera using the CSI ribbon cable.

Route the ribbon cable carefully to avoid sharp bends.

---

## Step 4 – Install MEMS Microphone

Connect the SPH0645 microphone to the Raspberry Pi GPIO.

Verify all I2S connections before powering on.

---

## Step 5 – Install Amplifier

Mount the PAM8403 amplifier.

Connect:

- Power
- Audio Input
- Left Speaker
- Right Speaker

---

## Step 6 – Install Speakers

Secure both speakers.

Verify correct polarity before final assembly.

---

## Step 7 – Power Connections

Connect:

Romoss Power Bank

↓

USB On/Off Switch

↓

Baseus USB-C Cable

↓

Raspberry Pi

Do not power on yet.

---

# 8. Software Installation

## Install Raspberry Pi OS

Flash Raspberry Pi OS onto the microSD card.

Insert the card into the Raspberry Pi.

Power on the system.

---

## Update the System

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

---

## Install Git

```bash
sudo apt install git
```

---

## Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/HoloJARVIS.git
```

```bash
cd HoloJARVIS
```

---

## Install Python Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Configure Environment

Create:

```
.env
```

Configure:

- API Keys
- Network Settings
- Voice Settings
- Camera Settings

---

## Start Backend

```bash
python main.py
```

or

```bash
uvicorn app:app
```

